---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import BaseLayout from "../components/BaseLayout.astro";
import notebook from "../assets/ink-notebook.webp";
---
<BaseLayout title="About Arman Mishra | Enkidu" description="Arman Mishra’s background in penetration testing, security research, tool development, and CTFs.">
  <header class="page-hero container">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Arman Mishra <span class="hero-accent">Known online as Enkidu.</span></h1>
    <p class="lead">Penetration tester, security researcher, and cybersecurity student at Lovely Professional University.</p>
  </header>
  <section class="container content-layout section">
    <figure class="about-art">
      <Image src={notebook} alt="An ink pen resting on an open notebook beside a rain-streaked window" widths={[380, 680, 950]} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 92vw, 420px" quality={72} loading="lazy" />
    </figure>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What I work on</h2>
      <p>I hold the <a href="/certifications/">CPTS and PJPT certifications</a> and am pursuing a Bachelor of Computer Applications with a specialization in Cyber Security. My hands-on work spans web applications, networks, Windows, Linux, and Active Directory.</p>
      <p>In CTFs, I’ve worked on both sides of the challenge. I’ve competed nationally and helped build forensic challenges and boot-to-root machines for HackVerse. I’ve also independently researched and disclosed vulnerabilities.</p>
      <h2>What I build</h2>
      <p>I wrote <a href="/projects/shredder/">Shredder</a> to organize the evidence produced during service enumeration. <a href="/projects/ink/">Ink</a> grew out of a different problem: keeping identities and authentication observations together across an assessment. I built an <a href="/projects/active-directory-lab/">Active Directory lab</a> to study how Windows configuration and identity affect the reach of a security issue.</p>
      <h2>Where I’m headed</h2>
      <p>I want to deepen my work in red-team operations and security research, especially around authentication and the trust relationships between services.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
